      "date": "1970-05-07",
      "kind": "planning decision",
      "description": "An automobile service station occupied the corner lot, used as a station site for more than 40 years; of the adjoining lots to the south, one held an abandoned single-family house and two were vacant. The City Planning Commission approved reclassifying the service station corner and adjoining lots from R-4 to C-2, allowing the station to be rebuilt and expanded as a Phillips Petroleum Company outlet.",
